        "value": "Here is a basic implementation of a Trie data structure with added functionality for managing frequencies of added words in Java:

```java
import java.util.*;

class TrieNode {
    int frequency;
    Map<Character, TrieNode> children;
    boolean isEndOfWord;

    public TrieNode() {
        frequency = 0;
        children = new HashMap<>();
        isEndOfWord = false;
    }
}

public class Trie {

    TrieNode root;

    public Trie() {
        root = new TrieNode();
    }

    public void addWord(String word, int frequency) {
        TrieNode node = root;
        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            node = node.children.computeIfAbsent(word.charAt(i), c -> new TrieNode());
        }
        node.isEndOfWord = true;;
        node.frequency = frequency;
    }

    public boolean searchWord(String word) {
        TrieNode node = root;
        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            char ch = word.charAt(i);
            if (node.children.containsKey(ch)) {
                node = node.children.get(ch);
            } else {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return node.isEndOfWord;
    }

    public int searchFrequency(String word) {
        TrieNode node = root;
        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            char ch = word.charAt(i);
            if (node.children.containsKey(ch)) {
                node = node.children.get(ch);
            } else {
                return -1;
            }
        }
        if (node.isEndOfWord)
            return node.frequency;
        else
            return -1;
    }

    public void deleteWord(String word) {
        deleteWord(root, word, 0);
    }

    public boolean deleteWord(TrieNode current, String word, int index) {
        if (index == word.length()) {
            if (!current.isEndOfWord) {
                return false;
            }
            current.isEndOfWord = false;
            current.frequency = 0;
            return current.children.isEmpty();
        }
        char ch = word.charAt(index);
        TrieNode node = current.children.get(ch);
        if (node == null) {
            return false;
        }
        boolean shouldDeleteCurrentNode = deleteWord(node, word, index + 1) && !node.isEndOfWord;
        if (shouldDeleteCurrentNode) {
            current.children.remove(ch);
            return current.children.isEmpty();
        }
        return false;
    }

    public void findAllWordsWithPrefix(String prefix) {
        TrieNode trieNode = root;
        for(int i=0; i<prefix.length(); i++) {
            char ch = prefix.charAt(i);
            TrieNode node = trieNode.children.get(ch);
            if(node == null)
                return;
            trieNode = node;
        }
        findAllChildWords(trieNode, prefix);
    }

    private void findAllChildWords(TrieNode trieNode, String word) {
        if(trieNode.isEndOfWord)
            System.out.println(word + " " + trieNode.frequency);
        for (char ch : trieNode.children.keySet())
            findAllChildWords(trieNode.children.get(ch), word + ch);
    }

    public void updateFrequency(String word, int freq) {
        TrieNode trieNode = root;
        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {
            if(trieNode.children.containsKey(c)){
                trieNode = trieNode.children.get(c);
            } else {
                return;
            }
        }
        if(trieNode.isEndOfWord){
            trieNode.frequency = freq;
        }  
    }
}
```

This code implements a very basic Trie class. The class contains methods for adding words with their associated frequencies to the Trie (`addWord()`), checking if a word is in the Trie and returning its frequency (`searchWord()`, `searchFrequency()`), deleting words from the Trie (`deleteWord()`), finding all words with a given prefix (`findAllWordsWithPrefix()`) and updating the frequency of a word (`updateFrequency()`). 

It's worth mentioning that this implementation assumes the words and prefixes are all in lower case since it doesn't handle case sensitivity."
